NNOOTTEESS
       On 4.3BSD, the ssiiggnnaall() function provided reliable semantics  (as  when
       calling  ssiiggvveecc()  with _v_e_c_._s_v___m_a_s_k equal to 0).  On System V, ssiiggnnaall()
       provides  unreliable  semantics.   POSIX.1  leaves  these  aspects   of
       ssiiggnnaall() unspecified.  See ssiiggnnaall(2) for further details.

       In  order  to  wait  for  a  signal,  BSD  and System V both provided a
       function named ssiiggppaauussee(3), but this function has a different  argument
       on the two systems.  See ssiiggppaauussee(3) for details.

